      "releaseNotes": "YOUR BACKUPS AT A GLANCE\nThe main screen is rebuilt around what's most relevant: whether a backup is running, how long it will take, and what all your backups have added up to.\n\nMIRRORING\nPhotos and Files backups can now follow your library and folders: items you delete leave the backup too. A Deleted folder keeps them first, for as long as you choose.\n\nMADE FOR IPHONE DUO\nThe main screen meets the fold with the status on one half and the controls on the other, and fits the outer screen when closed.\n\nSHORTCUTS AND SIRI, REIMAGINED\nA new Start Backup action replaces Start Photo Backup and Start File Backup, joined by actions to stop a backup and ask how it is going. Your existing shortcuts keep working.\n ALSO IN THIS UPDATE\n• The Live Activity has been redesigned.\n• Much improved error reporting.\n• New progress sounds. You can turn them off in Settings.\n• Many other small improvements and bug fixes.\n• Version 2.0.1: Minor fixes and new screenshots.\n\nVersion 2.0.2\n• New: Option to keep deleted items forever.\n• Fixed a crash shortly after starting a backup.\n• More reliable mirroring, free space and progress for network share Destinations.",
